---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ProductWordmark from '../components/ProductWordmark.astro';
import WorkflowFigure from '../components/WorkflowFigure.astro';
import { products } from '../data/products.mjs';
import { components } from '../data/components.mjs';
import { allMethods } from '../data/methods.mjs';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const ordered = ['vibe-sketch','vibe-queue','vibe-qc','vibe-view'].map(id => products.find(p => p.id === id));
---
<Base>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="technical-hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">The scientific toolset</span>
        <h1>From structure<br />to <em>understanding.</em></h1>
        <p>Sketch a molecule. Submit the job. Calculate its properties. Analyze the result.</p>
        <p class="hero-detail">Four independent tools for computational chemistry, with the methods, interfaces and documentation to connect them.</p>
        <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn primary" href={`${base}get-started`}>Start working <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn ghost" href={`${base}documentation/`}>Read the documentation</a></div>
      </div>
      <WorkflowFigure />
    </section>
    <div class="technical-strip"><div class="wrap"><span>MOLECULES & PERIODIC SOLIDS</span><span>PYTHON · CLI · BROWSER</span><a href="https://github.com/vibe-qc/qvf">QVF FORMAT ↗</a><a href="/docs/validation.html">DOCUMENTED VALIDATION ↗</a></div></div>
    <section class="block wrap" id="tools">
      <div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Tools</span><h2>Choose your starting point.</h2></div><p>Use one tool or connect several.<br />Each has its own installation and releases.</p></div>
      <div class="tool-grid">
        {ordered.map((p,i) => <article class={`tool-card tool-${p.id}`}>
          <div class="tool-card-top"><span>0{i+1} / {p.action}</span><span class="tool-state">{p.status || 'Independent tool'}</span></div>
          <h3><ProductWordmark product={p.id} label={p.name} /></h3><p>{p.summary}</p>
          <div class="tool-card-links"><a href={`${base}products/${p.id}/`}>{p.status ? 'Overview & access' : 'Technical overview'} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{p.docs && <a href={p.docs}>Manual ↗</a>}</div>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="science-section"><div class="wrap science-grid">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">02 / The calculation engine</span><h2>Molecules. <br />Materials. <br /><em>Methods with context.</em></h2><p>vibe-qc combines a Python interface with a C++17 electronic-structure engine. Choose a method by its documented scope, approximations and validation.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}methods/`}>Explore {allMethods.length} method families ↗</a></div>
      <div class="science-list">
        <a href="/docs/features.html"><span>01</span><div><h3>Molecular electronic structure</h3><p>Hartree–Fock and DFT, correlation, excited states and multireference methods.</p></div><b>↗</b></a>
        <a href="/docs/user_guide/periodic_systems.html"><span>02</span><div><h3>Periodic systems</h3><p>1D, 2D and 3D HF and KS-DFT, k-point sampling, bands and densities of states.</p></div><b>↗</b></a>
        <a href="/docs/tutorial/index.html"><span>03</span><div><h3>Properties & workflows</h3><p>Geometry optimization, spectra, reaction paths, solvent and bonding analysis.</p></div><b>↗</b></a>
        <a href={`${base}methods/`}><span>04</span><div><h3>Explicit status</h3><p>Production, preview, experimental and gated. AICCM/CCM and SECCM remain experimental.</p></div><b>↗</b></a>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="block wrap">
      <div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / Work from an example</span><h2>A practical route into the software.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}workflows/`}>All workflows ↗</a></div>
      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="/vibe-sketch/docs/quickstart.html"><span class="resource-index">01 / SKETCH</span><h3>Draw a structure. Prepare an input.</h3><p>Start with the sketcher’s testing version, export a figure or prepare a 3D calculation.</p><span class="text-link">Read the sketcher quickstart ↗</span></a>
        <a href="/vibe-queue/docs/user/index.html"><span class="resource-index">02 / SUBMIT</span><h3>Send the job to the queue</h3><p>Choose a configured host, submit the input and follow the job’s progress.</p><span class="text-link">Follow the job guide ↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}get-started#first-calculation`}><span class="resource-index">03 / CALCULATE</span><h3>Your first molecular calculation</h3><p>Install the engine, run Hartree–Fock on water and read the energy.</p><span class="text-link">Run the example ↗</span></a>
        <a href="/vibe-view/docs/quickstart.html"><span class="resource-index">04 / ANALYZE</span><h3>Open a result in vibe-view</h3><p>Inspect structures, orbitals, densities and spectra, or try the viewer with a bundled example.</p><span class="text-link">Open the walkthrough ↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="version-section"><div class="wrap version-grid">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">04 / Versions & availability</span><h2>Know what you are running.</h2><p>The website follows current source. The core manual follows qualified releases. Companions have their own version line.</p><p>Install from source or check each project’s release page. Container and desktop candidates on this site remain a <a href={`${base}download`}>Distribution preview</a>.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/changelog.html">Read the core changelog ↗</a></p></div>
      <div class="version-table"><h3>Engine and companion projects</h3>{components.map(c => <div><strong>{c.name}</strong>{c.version ? <span class="cmp-version">{c.version}</span> : <a href={c.releases}>Releases ↗</a>}<small>{c.role}</small></div>)}<div><strong>vibe-sketch</strong><a href={`${base}products/vibe-sketch/`}>Testing version ↗</a><small>Structure & reaction sketcher · proprietary</small></div><p>Core and basis numbers identify this source snapshot, not a new release announcement.</p></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="wrap closing-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">Built for reproducible work</span><h2>Read the methods. Keep the provenance.</h2><p>Find validation evidence, cite the algorithms you use, and share the files behind a result.</p></div><div><a class="text-link" href="/docs/validation.html">Validation & references ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}sponsor`}>Support the project ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}contact`}>Technical questions & access ↗</a></div></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
